@meeting train.m7.torres-zeke
// Pillar 5, M7, if Torres teaches it (a save where the row opens on a day he's on shift). Head writer, seat W.
title: Torres's old scanner
from: Zeke Torres
gist: Zeke gave you his old scanner. It reads a machine's parts, so you can choose which one to fetch.
== lines
torres-zeke: Got you something. Well. Got you something old.   [gesture]
torres-zeke > you: My first scanner. Mine's older than you, I said to Calder. She said "everything is".
torres-zeke: Press it to a panel. Every part gets a bar and a word.
torres-zeke: Good, worn, low, failing. Usually one's clearly sulking. That's your part.
torres-zeke: Two low? Use your eyes. What does the card say? What do you see up close?
torres-zeke: Wrong pick, you walk back. Happens to all of us. Me, twice on Tuesday.
? choice
* Are you sure? It's yours.   rel:torres-zeke+2 flavour:listen
  torres-zeke: It's been in my locker a year. It wants a job. Go on.   [laugh]
* Two low parts. How do I pick?   rel:torres-zeke+1 flavour:practical
  torres-zeke: Look before you scan. Cold door, seal. Cold oven, element.
* Thanks, Zeke.   rel:torres-zeke+1 flavour:cheer
  torres-zeke: Look after it. That's thanks enough.   [nod]
torres-zeke: Right. I'll read the first one. You watch. Then it's yours.
